#!/bin/bash
# Managed by Ansible (sf_dev role). Local edits are overwritten.
# Every boot, idempotent: home, the shared "fusion" network, the team guide.
set -e
if [ ! -d /home/dev ]; then
  mkdir -p /home/dev && cp -rT /etc/skel /home/dev && chown -R dev:dev /home/dev
fi
install -d -o dev -g dev -m 2775 /srv/sensor-fusion
docker network inspect fusion >/dev/null 2>&1 || docker network create fusion >/dev/null
[ -f /srv/sensor-fusion/PORTS.md ] || cat > /srv/sensor-fusion/PORTS.md <<'PORTS'
# Ports on sf-dev (claim one before you publish it)

| port | service | team | who |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1883 | MQTT broker (planned) | | |
PORTS
chown dev:dev /srv/sensor-fusion/PORTS.md
cat > /home/dev/README <<'GUIDE'
sf-dev: the Sensor Fusion box (TAK + Detection)
================================================
A small Ubuntu 24.04 machine on the tailnet with its own Docker. Build and run
your team's containers here; everything stays when the box restarts or is
rebuilt (system, Docker images and volumes, your files), backed up nightly.

Where things go
  ~/                      your scratch space (shared login: everyone is "dev")
  /srv/sensor-fusion/     the teams' services: one folder per team / service
  /srv/sensor-fusion/PORTS.md   claim a port before you publish it

Run a service
  cd /srv/sensor-fusion/<team>/<service>
  docker compose up -d --build        (add restart: unless-stopped to keep it up)
  docker compose logs -f              docker ps

Talk to each other
  - Containers on the shared network "fusion" reach each other by name:
      networks: { fusion: { external: true } }   ->  mqtt://mqtt:1883
  - Anyone in Sensor Fusion (laptops, phones with ATAK/iTAK, Pis, sensors)
    reaches a published port on sf-dev at  sf-dev:<port>  (tailnet IP: tailscale ip -4):
      ports: ["1883:1883"]
  - Not reachable from the internet; only the tailnet.

Keep data
  Named Docker volumes or files under /srv/sensor-fusion are kept and backed up.

Long-running things
  Use restart: unless-stopped in compose, or a systemd unit (systemctl works).

Limits (shared by everyone): {{ sf_dev_cpus | float | int }} CPUs, {{ sf_dev_memory }} RAM, {{ sf_dev_disk_size }} disk.
Admins: Survivability (Jake, Marcel).
GUIDE
chown dev:dev /home/dev/README
